        "σ C1-H24 -> π C1-C2",
        "π C2-N4 -> lp N4"
      ],
      "explanationAfterStep": "Losing the last proton makes the five-membered ring aromatic: an indole, here 1,2,3,4-tetrahydrocarbazole."
    }
  ],
  "mechanismSummary": "After the [3,3]-rearrangement (Part 1), the aniline NH₂ group adds to the iminium carbon and closes a five-membered ring. Proton transfers through acetic acid turn the other nitrogen into an NH₃⁺ group, which the ring nitrogen lone pair pushes out as ammonia. Loss of the last C–H proton gives the aromatic indole: 1,2,3,4-tetrahydrocarbazole.",
  "references": [
    "Clayden, Greeves and Warren, Organic Chemistry, 2nd edition (Oxford University Press), chapter 30"
  ],
